  "why": "The statement asks whether GCH alone proves diamond on the whole set E^{λ⁺}_{cf λ} for every singular λ. Every positive result in the record adds a hypothesis GCH does not give (□_λ for Shelah 1984, □*_κ for Zeman), so they settle a changed question: variant, not case. Gitik–Rinot get failure of diamond only on a stationary subset S at ℵ_ω, which does not contradict diamond on the whole set unless E∖S is nonstationary, and the record does not establish that; Rinot's survey still lists the question as open after citing it, so I read it as a variant (weaker conclusion) rather than a counterexample. Shelah 2007 is the source of the problem and explicitly leaves it unresolved; the survey restates it. All post-snapshot items concern approachability, regular cardinals, pcf, or a ZF model, so they bear on the question only as neighbouring work: none. No AI involvement anywhere.",
